Package: squidSim
Title: Flexible and Reproducible Structured Simulations
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Joel"    , "Pick"           , email = "joel.l.pick@gmail.com"             , role = c("aut","cre")),
    person("Hassen"  , "Allegue"        , email = "h.all@disroot.org"                 , role = "aut"))
Description: Simulates hierarchical and multivariate data from (generalised) linear mixed effects models, including additive genetic, phylogenetic and other covariance structures, and samples from the simulated populations in different ways. Helps researchers to become familiar with multilevel variation and to build sampling designs for their study. Builds on the Statistical Quantification of Individual Differences (SQuID) framework of Allegue et al. (2017) <doi:10.1111/2041-210X.12659> and Pick et al. (2025) <doi:10.32942/X20M0T>.
URL: https://github.com/squidgroup/squidSim
BugReports: https://github.com/squidgroup/squidSim/issues
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Imports:
    stats,
    Matrix,
    methods,
    MCMCglmm,
    mvnfast
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
